3b Every fitted line on boards A to E (grade_check), every module and every line no grade row covers. Rating: the grade row's
   maker's range with its category (SESSION rule, read from the row's clause and quote: rec, recommended; ec, the range the
   electrical characteristics hold over; op, operating as printed; dist, a distributor's parametric figure; abs, an absolute
   rating: the clause names maximum ratings or limiting values, a junction-and-storage or power-dissipation row, a junction row
   whose table the quote does not name (the conservative reading), or a distributor's figure for a TI power FET, whose held
   sheets print it as the absolute junction-and-storage row; abs rows are exclusion screens: INCONCLUSIVE when cleared). Board
   D's TUSB2046I is judged on the held TI sheet's recommended TA (p.6), its grade row's +115 C junction being its absolute row.
   Rise: the part's own over its local air (class named); local bounds with the rise. Board P and the cells are outside the
   chamber in E3-O and E5 (TEST-PLAN section 6): FEA-008's, not here. Lines read one by one carry 3a's verdict and category.
   categories of the screened lines: abs 33, dist 9, ec 13, op 77, rec 31, stor 5
   E3-O: INCONCLUSIVE 44, NO PART 3, NOT FITTED 1, NOT REACHED 112, OUT OF SCOPE 7, PLACEMENT 2, REACHED 10; E5: INCONCLUSIVE 45, NO PART 3, NOT FITTED 1, NOT REACHED 108, OUT OF SCOPE 7, PLACEMENT 6, REACHED 9
