3d FINDING, in the envelope as well (the generators' own declarations): board E's U13 is a TLV75533 in SOT-23-5 (DBV, 231.1 C/W,
   recommended junction +125 C, absolute +150 C, MAKER, TLV755P sheet, held back) on a rail declared at 0.35 A typical and 0.60 A
   peak from 5.0 V: 0.595 W, +137.5 K, past its recommended +125 C at any local air above -12.5 C; the declared peak exceeds its 500 mA
   output. Board C's U5 (the same part) is declared 0.149 A typical and 0.720 A peak, the peak past 500 mA. Even at the model's plan
   load U13 passes its recommended junction at both margins (3c): the regulators are part of the route (5c).

4 Three complete approaches for the parts that collide (the same margins, the same floor, the same ballasts, the plan heat)
   Common to all three (none can be done by the air, the physics of 4a): the SGP41's own shutdown at the margins and its
   in-envelope function (5d, the owner's question of 6); the MAIN, PI and TEST pushbuttons to a +85 C part; PDi's storage
   statement for the e-paper; board E's and board C's 3.3 V regulators (5c); the +70 C parts out of the running cooler's
   exhaust; the fans, the other lines with no range held and the lines cleared only by an absolute rating (7).
4a (a) THE HEAT PATH AND THE ENCLOSURE, no new mode: the heat stage at both margins, the radios on at both. Each part routed by
   the air needs (MODELED, E3-O / E5):
      RB9704    1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      LIME      1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      SA868     1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      PCM2912A  1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      G6K       1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      H5007NL   1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      ATP16     1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      PXP4043C  1.806 / 2.709 W/K
      SGP41     1.806 / 2.709 W/K  (its absolute rating's screen only: survival INCONCLUSIVE)
      XENARC    1.083 / 1.354 W/K
      CM5       0.903 / 1.083 W/K
      SOUNDER   0.903 / 1.083 W/K
      NVME      0.903 / 1.083 W/K
      AW7915    0.774 / 0.903 W/K
      RM520N    0.774 / 0.903 W/K
   so the line is 2.709 W/K (0 K margin), 3.010 with 1 K and 3.386 with 2 K; E3-O alone 1.806 W/K. It lies over the low case's
   outer-film cap (2.10 W/K) and under W4's high case (2.85 W/K finite inside film, 3.86 infinite); 32.53 gives 3.0 to 3.3.
   Not routed by the air (the air cannot be cooled below the ambient without a cooler, and a cooler in the sealed case returns
   its input to the air, L4-E10's corrected balance):
      ATP19     its limit 55 C (operating, powered) is at or under E3-O's ambient
      EPAPER    its limit 60 C (operating, unpowered, inside a range it may operate in (INFERRED to cover it unpowered)) is at or under E5's ambient
   Coupling the +70 C modules to the plate instead: the plate at E5 is 67.6..71.8 C at the floor; it needs 1.963 W/K at the plate's
   upper fraction, and the parts that cannot be coupled still need the line above. VERDICT: CONDITIONAL on T-H1 at or over
   2.709 W/K; not selected (0.55 W/K over (c)); it is what applies, with no hold, if T-H1 reads at or over it.
4b (b) WIDER-RATED PARTS, the mode and the enclosure unchanged (the inside air 76.25 C at E5, 81.89 C in the exhaust):
