                          +-1 W: 2.609 to 2.809 W/K; the limit +-1 K (or the ambient -+1 K): 2.462 to 3.010 W/K
   E5's heat under the hold, built up (MODELED, pwr_budget.py and pwr_red2.py as reproduced in 0, plan): 14.671 W at the load
   pins, 3.445 W lost in the converters, 0.036 W in the distribution (fuses, FETs, shunt, leads): 18.152 W at the pack; on shore
   the front end's and the charger's loss on it adds 1.345 W: 19.497 W into the case; L4-E8's ballasts add 2.09 W at the bound's
   worst corner (MODELED by L4-E8, ripple_dense.out, read): 21.587 W. The ambient 60 C is E5's dwell (Table 507.6-IX, 30 to 60
   C, the dwell from 0200 to 0800, 6 h, transcribed in mil-std-810h-method-507-6.md). The limit +70 C is the class the hold
   leaves in the air at E5 (each at its limit by 1j):
      RB9704 off +70 C (operating); LIME off +70 C (storage); SA868 off +70 C (operating); PCM2912A off +70 C (recommended); G6K off +70 C (operating); SGP41 off +50 C (recommended (Table 4)); H5007NL on +70 C (operating); ATP16 on +70 C (operating); PXP4043C off +70 C (operating)
