8d T-H1: WHO AND HOW. TEST-PLAN section 8's row: "a current-moulding Peli 1450 with the 1450PF frame and a 3 mm aluminium plate
   blank; 20, 40 and 60 W of resistive heat on a dummy stack, the fans running and stopped, lid open and closed, thermocouples
   on the air, the plate, the walls and a dummy pack block"; "it needs no built kit, and its purchase is the owner's to
   authorise". Hardware (READY-TO-ACT.md 5.2): the Peli 1450 with the 1450PF frame and a 3 mm plate blank, stack heaters of 6.8
   ohm at 12.0 V giving 21.2 W each, Pico Technology PicoLog TC-08, SKU PP222, 8 thermocouple inputs, "Same Sky CFM-6025BG68, 12
   V, the -22 variant (tachometer and PWM)". No electronics are needed. Who: the prototype bench, as Layer 9's physical
   verification, once the owner authorises it (READY-TO-ACT lists what is missing: "who runs the test and where (the session
   cannot)"); a laboratory only for a chamber run at E5's +60 C (the owner's spend). The draft procedure is
   T-H1-PROCEDURE-DRAFT.md beside this record.
   Method: the dummy heaters spread as the model spreads E5's hold (W, plan): board B (slot 3, its switch, hubs, supervisors,
   the device rail) 12.06; fans (the real fans, run from the bench supply) 1.95; board A 1.81; board C and the face 1.50; the
   front end and the charger (boards E and A, on shore) 1.35; board E 0.83, plus the ballasts' 2.09 W on board A; one heater's
   21.2 W puts the line's 9.8 K rise on the air (two: 19.6 K). Points: two powers (21.2 and 42.4 W), lid open and closed, fans
   on and off: 8 points. Steady state: the time constant C/G is 0.78 to 2.27 h (32.53's 8 to 10 kJ/K, the kit's mass, an upper
   bound for an empty case, over W4's lid-open 1.22 to 2.85 W/K); within 1 % of the rise after 3.6 to 10.5 h a point, 29 to 84 h
   in all; a point ends when the mixed air drifts at most 0.1 K/h over an hour (ASSUMPTION).
   Uncertainty (ASSUMPTION, standard, k = 1): each thermocouple +-0.2 K after an isothermal comparison, the mixed air's spread
   +-0.3 K, the ambient's drift +-0.3 K, the steady-state residual 0.129 K (the drift times the line's 1.29 h), so the rise
   +-0.526 K; the power +-0.7 %, the leads +-0.5 %. Expanded (k = 2): 10.7 % at a 10 K rise and 5.5 % at 20 K. PASS LINE: the
   measured conductance, lid open with the fans, less its expanded uncertainty, at or over 2.159 W/K, so a reading of at least
   2.416 W/K at a 10 K rise (2.285 W/K at 20 K). A room reading under-reads the margin: the outside films' radiation is 5.21
   W/m2K at the room's 22 C and 7.45 W/m2K at E5's 60 C, so on W4's films the margin's conductance is 1.15 to 1.20 times the
   room's (INFERRED, a credit the pass line does not take).
8e A FAILED READING AND THE FALLBACKS. Mixed air at a lid-open, fans-on reading G (MODELED; E3-O the heat stage, E5 the hold):
      G 2.100 W/K: E3-O 67.90 C (holds), E5 70.28 C (past +70 C)
      G 2.000 W/K: E3-O 68.54 C (holds), E5 70.79 C (past +70 C)
      G 1.900 W/K: E3-O 69.26 C (holds), E5 71.36 C (past +70 C)
      G 1.806 W/K: E3-O 70.00 C (holds), E5 71.95 C (past +70 C)
      G 1.666 W/K: E3-O 71.25 C (past +70 C), E5 72.95 C (past +70 C)
      G 1.500 W/K: E3-O 73.06 C (past +70 C), E5 74.39 C (past +70 C)
   A reading in (1.806, 2.159) W/K: E3-O holds as stated, E5 under the hold passes +70 C for the class of 8a. A reading under
   1.806 W/K: E3-O passes it too. The fallbacks inside the rulings (no vent, the Peli 1450 kept), each with what it buys:
   F1 FINS ON THE PLATE (no penetration; bonded or machined; INFERRED from W4's films, k the effective area multiplier): G for
      (inside k, outside k) = (1, 1) 1.222, (1, 1.5) 1.314, (1, 2) 1.376, (1, 3) 1.453, (2, 2) 1.667, (3, 3) 2.111 in the low
      case and (1, 1) 2.850, (1, 1.5) 3.062, (1, 2) 3.224, (1, 3) 3.453, (2, 2) 3.568, (3, 3) 4.286 in the high case; outside
      fins alone saturate at the inside film (1.690 and 4.411 W/K with an endless outside area). Applied to a reading through
      W4's split, outside fins of twice the area multiply it by 1.125 to 1.131 and fins of twice the area on both faces by 1.252
      to 1.363: a reading of 1.806 W/K would read 2.261 to 2.462 W/K (both faces). T-H1's plate and wall readings give the split
      the reading actually has. Feasibility: CONDITIONAL on the face's free area (the monitor, the e-paper, the switches) and
      the lid's clearance (CASE-MARGINS M3); the session's (Layer 7).
   F2 CONDUCTION FROM THE HOT BOARDS TO THE PLATE: heat Q_c led into the plate leaves the air's balance by Q_c (1 - f), f the
      plate's fraction, so E5 at +70 C needs Q_c = (Q - 10 G) / (1 - f): G 2.000: 5.76 / 2.97; G 1.900: 9.39 / 4.84; G 1.806:
      12.82 / 6.60 (W at f 0.725 / 0.465). Board B carries 12.06 W of the hold's heat (the module, its switch, the supervisors,
      the hubs). Feasibility: CONDITIONAL on a pad path from those parts to the plate (Layer 7); the session's.
   F3 SHEDDING IN E5 (E5 requires logging only): the heat a reading allows, 10 G - 2.09 W: G 2.100: 18.91 W; G 2.000: 17.91 W; G
      1.900: 16.91 W; G 1.806: 15.97 W; G 1.666: 14.57 W; G 1.500: 12.91 W. A deeper hold that keeps the logging (the module
      idle on its own storage, board E's controller and sensors, the fans, the panel for the SOS, the supervisors and hubs on
      the logging path) and turns off KSZ9897R AVDDL+DVDDL 1.2 V 1.452 W, KSZ9897R AVDDH 2.5 V 0.825 W, KSZ9897R VDDIO 3.3 V
      0.264 W, NVMe slot 3 0.900 W, PCIe switch 3.3 V slot 3 0.355 W, PCIe switch 1.0 V slot 3 0.270 W, LG290P GNSS 0.327 W
      takes E5's heat to 13.429 W and its line to 1.552 W/K. The session's (E5's stated configuration); CONDITIONAL on a supply
      switch for each (none read for the switch chip: a Layer 8 item) and on the logging path.
   F4 THE PLATE COUPLING (4e): the RockBLOCK, board D (SA868, PCM2912A, G6K) and the LimeSDR on pads to the plate sit at the
      plate, at most the ambient plus 0.725 of the rise: E5 holds them to 1.564 W/K and E3-O to 1.309 W/K. The parts left in the
      mixed air then set the floor: the +80 C connectors (2199119-3, 2199230-4, MDT420M02001, TYPE-C-31-M-12) in the exhaust
      need 1.253 W/K in E5 and 1.399 W/K in E3-O (1.083 out of the exhaust); the H5007NL, the ATP16 and the PXP4043/C take
      section 6's wider parts or statements. So F4 holds E5 down to 1.564 W/K and E3-O down to 1.399 W/K (1.309 with the
      connectors out of the exhaust); with F3, E5 down to 1.125 W/K. With the fans stopped the coupled parts stay at most 69.82
      C (8b). Feasibility: the pads' own rise and their mechanical path (Layer 7); the session's.
   THE BEST FALLBACK: F4, the plate coupling, with F3 in E5: no owner ruling, no change to E3-O. What needs the owner: a reading
   under E3-O's F4 floor (1.399 W/K, or 1.309 W/K with the connectors out of the exhaust) leaves a deviation of E3-O's
   configuration (the hold in E3-O) or a device-set re-pick (CHO-001); the SGP41 is 6b's question already.

9 THE CONSERVATIVE LOWER BOUND, AND U-02'S CLASS (the consolidation's question of 2 October 2026: does T-H1 confirm a design
  the evidence already supports, or decide whether it can work?)
9a THE MODEL. The inside air to the ambient through two paths in parallel, each solved for its heat at a stated air rise: the
   plate (the inside film, the 3 mm aluminium, the outside films; lid closed, the enclosed layer to the lid and the lid's shell)
   and the walls (the inside film, the PP shell, the outside films); the floor adiabatic (the case on its feet, 8.38 mm over a
   support whose temperature no document gives). Held geometry (CASE-MARGINS, Peli's drawing and STEP as read there; W4's plate
   outline): the plate 0.0912 m2 (L = A/P 0.0741 m); the walls 0.1296 m2 inside (the perimeter 377.75 x 263.45 mm at mid-height,
   floor to the shoulder at 101.04 mm) and 0.1444 m2 outside (the outer perimeter over the base's 108.97 mm), 5.34 mm thick; lid
   closed, the flat ceiling 0.0803 m2, the skirt 0.0578 m2, the layer 53.5 mm (W4's 46.5 to 53.5); the floor 0.0786 m2.
   Correlations (textbook, INFERRED): a plate facing up hot or down cold, Nu = 0.54 Ra^(1/4) (0.15 Ra^(1/3) over 1e7), L = A/P;
   a vertical wall, Churchill and Chu, Nu = {0.825 + 0.387 Ra^(1/6)/[1 + (0.492/Pr)^(9/16)]^(8/27)}^2; the enclosed layer,
   Hollands et al., Nu = 1 + 1.44[1 - 1708/Ra]+ + [(Ra/5830)^(1/3) - 1]+; radiation eps F sigma (T1^2 + T2^2)(T1 + T2) to
   surroundings at the ambient; air by Sutherland's laws. Coefficients, the end the bound takes first: the plate's emissivity
   0.70 (0.70 to 0.90, anodised), the shell's 0.85 (0.85 to 0.95, pigmented PP), the PP's conductivity 0.12 W/mK (0.12 to 0.22),
   the plate's view past the open lid 0.70 (0.70 to 1.00, ASSUMPTION); still air at the margin's ambient (a chamber's
   circulation not credited); inside, natural convection only: the fans' flow and the stack's radiation to the plate are
   credited at zero (no held document places or picks the fans), each shown below as a credit.
9b THE BOUND (W/K; lid open with the fans, their flow credited at zero; MODELED on INFERRED coefficients):
   E5    60 C, the air 10 K up: lid open 0.566 (the other coefficient ends 0.626), lid closed 0.505; plate fraction 0.348
         credits: the fans' flow 0.2 / 0.5 / 1.0 m/s 0.608 / 0.690 / 0.799; the stack's radiation 0.654, with 0.5 m/s 0.767; the floor 0.697; all the
         favourable ends with 1.0 m/s 1.145; a 50 m/s inside flow (a film near 45 W/m2K, not a zero inside resistance: 12e) 1.540
   E3-O  55 C, the air 15 K up: lid open 0.607 (the other coefficient ends 0.673), lid closed 0.537; plate fraction 0.362
         credits: the fans' flow 0.2 / 0.5 / 1.0 m/s 0.641 / 0.712 / 0.813; the stack's radiation 0.692, with 0.5 m/s 0.788; the floor 0.747; all the
         favourable ends with 1.0 m/s 1.168; a 50 m/s inside flow (a film near 45 W/m2K, not a zero inside resistance: 12e) 1.571
   The envelope's +40 C, the air 15 K up: lid open 0.598, lid closed 0.524 (LO-01a's and E3-L's state; U-01's, not this record's).
   The bound's films at E5 (W/m2K): inside, the plate 4.13 and the walls 3.85; outside, the face 7.72 and the walls 10.03.
9c W4'S 1.22 W/K RECONCILED. The budget's 1.22 to 2.85 W/K (lid open, fans) and 1.06 to 2.49 W/K (lid closed) are W4's lumped
   estimate (records/w4/w4-scratch-thermal.py, pwr_budget.py's G): fixed films, inside 10 to 25 W/m2K for "low-velocity forced
   flow from the mixer and cooler fans, plus internal radiation", outside 9.5 to 11.5 (the face), 8 to 10 (the walls), 3 to 8
   (the floor) at about 310 K with emissivities 0.85 to 0.9, the base's walls 0.1373 to 0.2200 m2, PP at 0.018 m2K/W. It is a
   sensitivity estimate, not a lower bound: its low end already assumes the fans' film. One assumption at a time, W4's low case
   to the bound (E5):
      W4's low case (lid open, fans)                                                                       1.222 W/K
      the floor adiabatic (the case on its feet)                                                           1.009 W/K
      the walls' inner area to the plate (CASE-MARGINS)                                                    0.977 W/K
      the wall 5.34 mm of PP at 0.12 W/mK                                                                  0.925 W/K
      the outer films at +60 C with the conservative emissivities and the lid's view                       0.928 W/K
      the inside film: natural convection only, no fan flow and no internal radiation credited             0.566 W/K
   The decisive term is the inside film: W4's low case takes 10 W/m2K with the fans; natural convection gives 3.85 to 4.13
   W/m2K, and no held document gives the fans' flow at the inner faces.
9d AGAINST THE LINES AND THE FALLBACK. The lines (2.159 W/K in E5, 1.806 W/K in E3-O) lie over the bound with a 50 m/s inside
   flow (1.540 and 1.571 W/K; CORRECTED in 12e: that flow's film is near 45 W/m2K, not a zero inside resistance, and the outside
   capacity proper at these rises is 1.856 and 1.906 W/K on the conservative ends, so E3-O's line lies under it and E5's over
   it, both under it at the optimistic ends). Section 8's floors (E5 1.125 W/K with F4 and F3; E3-O 1.399, or 1.309 with the
   connectors out of the exhaust) lie over the bound by 0.559 and 0.792 W/K. Where the air settles on the bound (MODELED, lid
   open, its own rise):
      E5, the hold: the air 90.93 C (0.698 W/K at 30.9 K), the plate 71.48 C; the +70 C class on the plate (F4) 71.48 C, PAST
         +70 C; the +80 C connectors in the exhaust 93.71 C, PAST +80 C; the +80 C connectors out of it 90.93 C, PAST +80 C; the
         module, +85 C at its intake (device set) 90.93 C, PAST +85 C.
      E5, the deeper hold (F3): the air 83.41 C (0.663 W/K at 23.4 K), the plate 68.58 C; the +70 C class on the plate (F4)
         68.58 C, inside; the +80 C connectors in the exhaust 86.19 C, PAST +80 C; the +80 C connectors out of it 83.41 C, PAST
         +80 C; the module, +85 C at its intake (device set) 83.41 C, inside.
      E3-O, the heat stage: the air 92.61 C (0.720 W/K at 37.6 K), the plate 69.22 C; the +70 C class on the plate (F4) 69.22 C,
         inside; the +80 C connectors in the exhaust 98.25 C, PAST +80 C; the +80 C connectors out of it 92.61 C, PAST +80 C;
         the module, +85 C at its intake (device set) 92.61 C, PAST +85 C.
   E5 with F4 and F3, with every session measure (F4, F3 in E5, the +80 C connectors to +85 C parts, the HX magnetics, the wider
   buttons): the module's +85 C binds, needing 0.621 W/K at its 25 K; the bound gives 0.671 W/K: clears by 0.050 W/K. Credits no
   held evidence bounds: internal radiation credited 0.764; the floor credited 0.824; internal radiation and the floor credited
   0.916; a forced flow across the inner faces is not needed.
   E3-O with F4, with every session measure (F4, F3 in E5, the +80 C connectors to +85 C parts, the HX magnetics, the wider
   buttons): the module's +85 C binds, needing 0.903 W/K at its 30 K; the bound gives 0.691 W/K: GAP 0.212 W/K. Credits no held
   evidence bounds: internal radiation credited 0.781; the floor credited 0.847; internal radiation and the floor credited
   0.938; a forced flow across the inner faces of 1.28 m/s alone would close it.
9e U-02'S CLASS: T-H1 DECIDES. On held geometry and conservative coefficients the sealed case does not hold E3-O as stated: with
   every measure inside the session's authority the module's intake reaches 92.61 C against its +85 C (a gap of 0.212 W/K); E5
   holds with them (0.050 W/K to spare). What could close the gap: the fans' flow at the inner faces (1.28 m/s, Layer 7's mixer
   placement) or the stack's radiation and the floor's support (with both credited the bound reads 0.938 W/K), all of which T-H1
   measures; leading the module's heat into the plate, which competes with F4 for the plate's outside (0.704 W/K at the bound's
   face film) and needs a finned plate the face's layout has not been shown to carry (Layer 7, unbounded); a deeper hold in E3-O
   (a deviation of E3-O's configuration) or a device-set re-pick (CHO-001), both the owner's. U-02 stays a closure condition of
   L4-E9's gate.
9f THE SMALLEST EXPERIMENT THAT RESOLVES IT: one point of T-H1, lid open, the fans running at full duty (the two mixers and slot
   3's cooler fan, stand-ins until D-18), one heater's 21.2 W spread as the hold spreads it (8d), at room temperature in still
   air; channels: the mixed air (four), the ambient (two), the plate's inner face, a wall's inner face (one logger). It runs to
   steady state, the mixed air drifting at most 0.1 K/h over an hour: 5.9 h at the line's conductance, up to 21.1 h if the case
   is as poor as the bound (time constant 4.57 h). G = P / rise; the readings that settle it, each the target plus its expanded
   uncertainty at that point's rise:
      a reading of at least 2.462 W/K (8.6 K rise) meets 2.159 W/K: E5's line, the design as stated (route (c))
      a reading of at least 1.516 W/K (14.0 K rise) meets 1.399 W/K: E3-O with F4, the connectors in the exhaust (section 8)
      a reading of at least 1.410 W/K (15.0 K rise) meets 1.309 W/K: E3-O with F4, the connectors out of the exhaust (section 8)
      a reading of at least 1.199 W/K (17.7 K rise) meets 1.125 W/K: E5 with F4 and F3 (section 8)
      a reading of at least 0.951 W/K (22.3 K rise) meets 0.903 W/K: E3-O with every session measure (the module's +85 C binds)
      a reading of at least 0.644 W/K (32.9 K rise) meets 0.621 W/K: E5 with every session measure (the module's +85 C binds)
   ACCEPTANCE: at or over 2.462 W/K the design holds as stated (route (c)); at or over 1.516 W/K section 8's fallback holds; at
   or over 0.951 W/K E3-O holds with every session measure, provided the measured plate fraction keeps the plate-coupled +70 C
   class inside (the plate fraction times 27.086 W over the reading, at most 15 K); under 0.951 W/K E3-O as stated cannot hold
   on the session's means and the owner decides (a deviation of E3-O or a re-pick). The room reading is the conservative side of
   the margin's (8d). The full T-H1 (eight points) follows for the fans-off case, the lid-closed state and the fractions.
9g THE FANS' POWER (13.3 confirmed): counted in pwr_budget.py, the 42.8 W profile, its replay and L4-E9's endurance (2.0 W in
   the hold, 3.1 W in the profile), not among the 8.4 W with no document. The bound credits their flow at zero and still counts
   their heat inside the case: nothing in 8c changes.

10 THE HEAT-REJECTION QUESTION (the consolidation, 2 October 2026: if T-H1 reads under what the approved profile needs, what
   change inside the rulings restores it at REQ-024's +40 C, and charging on the design day?)
10a THE NEED. The approved profile PS-IDLE-SPEC puts 43.413 W into the case lid open (MODELED: its 42.824 W at the pack plus the
   pack's own I2R; L4-E9's 43.4 W at a0212d9e). Its +70 C class at REQ-024's +40 C needs 1.447 W/K; a charge starts only while
   the gauge reads at or under 42 C (TEST-PLAN, T3), so on SC-37's design day (the air 13.2 to 18.3 C, the replay) charging with
   the profile running (52.134 W into the case, the balance of 12b) needs 1.810 to 2.200 W/K. The rulings: no vent or opening
   anywhere (32.53), the Peli 1450 at any cost, the face a 3 mm aluminium plate carrying the UI (32.40). Every figure below is
   on section 9's bound: the inside by natural convection only, the coefficients' conservative ends, still air; a two-node
   model, the inside air and the plate.
10b THE THREE APPROACHES. (a) Fins on the face's free strips (the plate 0.0912 m2 less the monitor window 0.0288 m2 and the
   e-paper lens 0.0071 m2: 0.0552 m2), fixed under M3's space beneath the QMX tray (19.92 mm nominal, 14.11 mm with the unstated
   allowances doubled) or a clip-on exchanger when deployed; effective area multiplier 2 to 3 (ASSUMPTION; a vendor's heat-sink
   datasheet gives the real one). (b) The large loads led into the plate by heat pipes, bars and gap pads, 23.641 W at their
   pins (Xenarc 709GNK 6.000, WiFi link card 1 (live) 4.000, CM5 slot 1 2.000, CM5 slot 2 2.000, CM5 slot 3 2.000, panel board C
   1.500, KSZ9897R AVDDL+DVDDL 1.2 V 1.452, KSZ9897R AVDDH 2.5 V 0.825, KSZ9897R VDDIO 3.3 V 0.264, NVMe slot 1 0.900, NVMe slot
   2 0.900, NVMe slot 3 0.900, VHF PA 30 W 0.900), so the plate rejects them at its own temperature and the air keeps the rest;
   with (a)'s fins. (c) The open lid as a second radiator: an aluminium skin on the lid's flat ceiling (0.0803 m2, an upper
   bound: the QMX tray and the tablet bracket share it), 0.329 m tall when open, on a copper braid from the plate's edge inside
   the seal line (0.20 m, 200 mm2: 2.56 K/W, ASSUMPTION; copper 390 W/mK). At the profile's heat at +40 C and the charging heat
   (52.134 W, 12b) on the design day (MODELED on the bound):
      approach                                 | +40 C: air, plate, G      | design day 13.2 C: air, G | 18.3 C: air, G
      none: the bound                          |  96.61 C  62.34 C  0.767 W/K |  80.37 C  0.776 W/K      |  85.28 C  0.778 W/K
      (a) fins on the free strips, k 2         |  92.89 C  56.15 C  0.821 W/K |  75.74 C  0.834 W/K      |  80.69 C  0.836 W/K
      (a) fins on the free strips, k 3         |  90.84 C  52.78 C  0.854 W/K |  73.16 C  0.869 W/K      |  78.15 C  0.871 W/K
      (b) the large loads led into the plate   |  79.59 C  70.08 C  1.096 W/K |  64.43 C  1.018 W/K      |  69.29 C  1.022 W/K
      (b) with (a)'s fins, k 3                 |  72.41 C  56.96 C  1.339 W/K |  55.76 C  1.225 W/K      |  60.71 C  1.229 W/K
      (c) the open lid's skin on a strap       |  94.17 C  58.27 C  0.801 W/K |  77.31 C  0.813 W/K      |  82.26 C  0.815 W/K
      (b) + (a) + (c): the best route          |  71.36 C  55.12 C  1.384 W/K |  54.46 C  1.263 W/K      |  59.43 C  1.268 W/K
   Needs: 1.447 W/K at +40 C (the air at 70 C); 1.810 and 2.200 W/K for charging (the air at 42 C). The open lid's strap carries
   4.37 W at +40 C in the best route.
10c CONSEQUENCES (all three passive: no power, no endurance change, the heat unchanged; costs TBD, no quote held). (a): about
   0.39 kg of 1.5 mm fins at an 8 mm pitch to the worst M3 height (ASSUMPTION), no inside space; the UI's strips between the
   monitor, the e-paper and the switches, the light guides kept clear; bonded fins keep the face a 3 mm plate (a SESSION
   reading), an extruded thicker face would change the ruling of 32.40 (the owner's); a clip-on exchanger needs stowage. (b):
   spreaders and pads under the plate in the 11.9 to 22.9 mm between board B's tall parts and the face parts (W4), their mass
   and cost TBD; the plate runs at 55.12 C (70.08 C without fins): the face's touch temperature rises (no held limit: an
   evaluation owed), the e-paper's +60 C operation is passed without fins, the switches go to +85 C parts, and each led part
   sits at the plate plus its path's drop (the WiFi card's +70 C bounds that drop); all inside the seal. (c): about 0.58 kg (a 1
   mm skin 0.22 kg, the braid 0.36 kg), the braid's fatigue over the hinge's cycles, the lid tray's layout; inside the seal
   line, no penetration.
10d THE SELECTION: NONE REACHES THE NEED ON BOUNDED EVIDENCE. The best route assembled from the three, (b) with (a)'s fins and
   (c), keeps the air at 71.36 C at +40 C: it rejects 42.161 W with the air at +70 C against the profile's 43.413 W, SHORT BY
   1.252 W (0.063 W/K). Charging with the profile running stays out of reach: 0.547 and 0.932 W/K short on the design day's cold
   and warm ends. On the bound alone the case rejects 20.449 W at +40 C (22.964 W short). What would carry the route over: the
   inside film the fans make (section 9: credited at zero), and the fins' and the path's real resistances; each is a measurement
   or a maker's datasheet, not held. The remaining options are the owner's: an ALTERNATIVE duty cycle at +40 C, labelled as such
   (PS-IDLE, the monitor dimmed and no beacon: 40.242 W into the case, under the best route's 42.161 W by 1.919 W, and nothing
   fits on the bound alone), or a requirement change (the profile's ambient ceiling, or charging with the profile running on the
   design day).
10e U-02 by the owner's exit definition: a CLOSURE CONDITION, with its exact fact: the sealed case's conductance lid open with
   the fans, as T-H1 reads it (the fans' inside film is what no document bounds). The smallest experiment: one point of T-H1,
   lid open, the fans at full duty, two heaters (42.4 W, about the profile's heat) spread as the boards dissipate, room air, to
   steady state (section 9f's duration). The readings that settle it (each the target plus its expanded uncertainty):
      a reading of at least 1.509 W/K (28.1 K rise) meets 1.447 W/K: the profile's +70 C class at +40 C (the consolidation's framing; section 11 reconciles it)
      a reading of at least 1.906 W/K (22.2 K rise) meets 1.810 W/K: charging with the profile on the design day's cold end
      a reading of at least 2.342 W/K (18.1 K rise) meets 2.200 W/K: charging with the profile on the design day's warm end
   Under the first, the route of 10d applies with its kit on the same bench point, and an owner's choice of 10d's options if it
   still reads short. (These readings take the 42.4 W of two heaters for every line and are superseded: 11a and 12d read each
   mode at its own heat, the fans counted, and 12a names each mode's governing line.)

11 THE THERMAL RECONCILIATION (the owner's amendment of 2 October 2026, 14:20, item 1)
11a THE CLAIM, CHECKED. Section 10e's line read: a reading of at least 1.509 W/K at 42.4 W meets 1.447 W/K. Its arithmetic: 42.4
   W / 1.509 W/K = 28.1 K at the bench; the expanded uncertainty at that rise is 4.12 % (k = 2), so the conductance after it is
   1.509 x (1 - 0.0412) = 1.447 W/K, which is the profile's 43.413 W over the 30 K from +40 C to the +70 C class. The owner's
   check is right that the same reading puts the air at 68.1 C at +40 C. What it establishes is narrower than "operation at +40
   C": the profile's own +70 C class at +40 C, a condition no requirement asks for, because at +40 C the kit does not run the
   profile: REQ-024: "on measured inside-air (+50 C) and cell (+55 C) temperatures the kit sheds to its reduced mode and then
   its heat stage (C1)"; D-02b: "above +35 C ambient the kit runs one module". The 1.447 W/K is nonetheless the profile's own
   condition at REQ-014's +20 C ("its battery-only runtime is stated in hours in an idle and a typical mode (PS-IDLE-SPEC and
   PS-TYP) at +20 C"): there the profile runs unshed only while the inside air stays under C1's +50 C, 43.413 W over 30 K.
11b THE HEAT, COUNTED ONCE (MODELED, plan). The profile PS-IDLE-SPEC: 36.448 W at the load pins (the five fans' own 2.97 W among
   them: the three modules' coolers and the two mixers), 6.376 W lost in the converters and the distribution, 0.590 W in the
   pack's own resistance: 43.413 W into the case. Not in it: L4-E8's ballasts (0.0093 W at its nominal illustration, at most
   2.09 W at the bound's worst corner, and only while the solar stage runs), the solar entry's sense bank (solar current only),
   Q39's 0.0945 W with L4-E11's (B1) (L4-E9 at a0212d9e). Charging with the profile running on the design day (the balance of
   12b, CORRECTED: the source path's loss on the profile's power was left out) adds 8.721 W: 52.134 W. The heat stage on shore:
   19.378 W at the pins (fans 1.95 W: slot 3's cooler and the two mixers), 3.893 W in the converters and the distribution, 1.725
   W in the front end and the charger, the ballasts 2.09 W (counted at the worst corner, the margins' rule): 27.086 W. The
   bench: READY-TO-ACT's heater is 6.8 ohm at 12.0 V, 21.176 W of heat (all of its electrical power stays inside); two give
   42.353 W. The fans run from the bench supply, their measured draw is heat inside and is added to the heaters: P = the heaters
   + the fans, never the heaters alone (section 10e's 42.4 W left the fans out and is restated here). To stand for a mode the
   heaters are set to its heat less the fans' measured draw: the profile 40.443 W (two heaters at 11.73 V), the heat stage
   25.136 W (one heater at 13.07 V); the fans' draw replaces their modeled share, so nothing is counted twice.
11c THE NODES AND THE LIMITS. The conductance is between two nodes: the mixed inside air (the mean of the air channels, the
   hold's reference placed in it, 4d) and the ambient air (shaded channels about 0.5 m from the case). The bench ambient is the
   room (+22 C taken); the operational ambient is REQ-024's "The kit operates at -20 to +40 C ambient". The limits and their
   references: C1's inside-air trigger +50 C and cell trigger +55 C (REQ-024, CONOPS 4: "C1, module shedding | inside air +50 C
   or any cell +55 C | normal to the reduced mode; reached again in the reduced mode, to the heat stage; restores 5 K below"),
   control triggers that shed, not damage limits; the SGP41's +55 C inside air (REQ-052: "every part inside its published range
   (an SGP41 above +55 C fails)"; TEST-PLAN E3-L: "the inside air at or under the SGP41's +55 C; an SGP41 above +55 C fails
   E3-L"), resting on its Table 5 absolute row, and its +50 C under this record's corrected rule (Table 4, section 5d, the
   owner's CFL-002); the +70 C class (the makers' sheets, section 4: RockBLOCK 9704, SA868, G6K, PCM2912A, LimeSDR, H5007NL,
   ATP16, PXP4043/C; the AW7915's 0 to +70 C operating while the profile runs it); the module's +85 C (CM5 p.28); the cells
   (E3-A: "no charge starts while the gauge reads above 42 C (T3)"; "every cell surface at most +60 C throughout"). REQ-024's
   acceptance: "part_temps.py finds no part outside its range". D-02a's +55 C is an AMBIENT qualification margin, not an
   inside-air limit: "TEST-PLAN's +55 C operating, +71 C storage and -33 C storage are QUALIFICATION MARGINS over the -20 to +40
   C use and -20 to +45 C storage envelope, with two pass lines: operate to specification inside the envelope; survive and
   recover at the margin."
   Each condition: requirement and mode, heat into the case, ambient, the limit at the node, and the conductance it needs (Q / room):
      K1   REQ-024 and E3-A at +40 C: C1's end state, the heat stage on shore with the ballasts; a SCREEN, not a closure line
           (12a); lid open; 27.086 W at +40.0 C; the SGP41's Table 5 +55 C, an ABSOLUTE rating (REQ-052's and E3-L's fail line
           reads it): an exclusion screen, never the sensor's function; needs 1.806 W/K
      K2   the same, the SGP41 judged on its Table 4 +50 C (this record's corrected rule; the owner's CFL-002 open); lid open;
           27.086 W at +40.0 C; the SGP41's +50 C (Table 4); needs 2.709 W/K
      K3   the same, the +70 C class in the heat stage (the H5007NL, the ATP16, the PXP4043/C and the radios C1 leaves on) at
           the MIXED air; a component screen (the exhaust, the cells and the junctions are 12a's); lid open; 27.086 W at +40.0
           C; +70 C (the makers' sheets of section 4); needs 0.903 W/K
      K4   the same, the module's intake; lid open; 27.086 W at +40.0 C; the module's +85 C (CM5 4.4); needs 0.602 W/K
      K5   REQ-052 and E3-L at +40 C: the heat stage; a SCREEN (12a); lid closed; 27.086 W at +40.0 C; the SGP41's Table 5 +55 C
           (E3-L's fail line; ABSOLUTE, a screen); needs 1.806 W/K
      K6   REQ-014 at +20 C: the profile on the pack, not shed by C1; lid open; 43.413 W at +20.0 C; C1's inside-air trigger +50
           C (REQ-024); needs 1.447 W/K
      K7   charging on SC-37's design day, the profile running, the balance of 12b (the source path, the charge path, the
           charging cells, the solar stage's ballasts), cold end; lid open; 52.134 W at +13.2 C; the gauge's charge start T3 42
           C (E3-A; the idle cells at the air; the running charge's T4 with the cells' own rise is 12a's); needs 1.810 W/K
      K8   the same, warm end; lid open; 52.134 W at +18.3 C; T3 42 C; needs 2.200 W/K
      K9   E3-O, D-02a's +55 C AMBIENT margin: the heat stage, every radio C1 leaves on; lid open; 27.086 W at +55.0 C; +70 C
