   M8 and M9). Section 2d's charge in E3-O keeps the charge path's 3.446 W only: the pack is outside the case there, its cells'
   I2R with it.
12c B7, THE BATTERY-ONLY RUN COUPLED TO C1 (MODELED, energy-and-thermal). The run: PS-IDLE-SPEC on the pack (42.824 W at the
   pack, 43.413 W into the case) from a kit soaked at +20 C, lid open, shaded, still air; C1 moves the kit to the reduced mode
   at the inside air's +50 C and, its trigger still holding at the next reading, to the heat stage (23.272 W at the pack, 23.446
   W into the case; CONOPS states no dwell between the two, the model takes none); the reduced mode's restore, 5 K under the
   trigger, is not reached; the run ends on the 35E's usable 107.9 Wh at the profile's rate (the shed states' slightly larger
   usable energy, energy_budget's PS-SURV-R row, not credited); the cells quasi-steady over the air by their own I2R over the
   block's lowest film; one node, C the kit's 8 to 10 kJ/K (32.53). The reviewer's constant-G check reproduced (C 8 kJ/K): G
   0.6711 W/K reaches C1 at 2.063 h and, unshed, the air 54.46 C at 2.52 h; G 0.7404 W/K reaches C1 at 2.151 h and, unshed, the
   air 53.31 C at 2.52 h.
   The enclosure model's own G(rise) (section 9, lid open), integrated in 10 s steps:
      the bound                      C  8.0 kJ/K: C1 at 2.01 h, then the heat stage for 0.94 h; the run 2.95 h; the air at most 51.21 C, the cells at most 53.99 C (H1 at 56.5 C not reached)
      the bound                      C 10.0 kJ/K: C1 at 2.51 h, then the heat stage for 0.01 h; the run 2.52 h; the air at most 50.02 C, the cells at most 53.99 C (H1 at 56.5 C not reached)
      the coefficients' other ends   C  8.0 kJ/K: C1 at 2.09 h, then the heat stage for 0.79 h; the run 2.88 h; the air at most 50.41 C, the cells at most 54.00 C (H1 at 56.5 C not reached)
